gaps.responseShape:
200 { data: { currencyCode: string, balanceMinor: string, balance: string, lowWatermarkMinor: string, isLow: boolean, checkedAt: string } }

Concrete example (mocks/db.ts:1557-1577):
{ "currencyCode": "NSP", "balanceMinor": "443750000", "balance": "4437500.00", "lowWatermarkMinor": "50000000", "isLow": false, "checkedAt": "2026-09-11T10:14:00.000Z" }

Field rules the console enforces: `balanceMinor` and `lowWatermarkMinor` MUST be integer decimal strings matching /^-?\d+$/ — a number, or "1320000.00", makes the pill render nothing (agent-float-pill.tsx:12,22). `balance` is the same figure preformatted via formatMinorToDecimal(). `checkedAt` is ISO-8601.

Rebuild recipe (copy from AgentFloatSyncService.ledgerFloat, agent-float-sync.service.ts:271-280):
  const account = await accounts.findByCode(prisma, ichancyAgentFloatCode(config.ichancy.currency));
  const balanceMinor = account === null ? 0n : await accounts.computeBalanceFromEntries(prisma, account.id);
  const watermark = config.limits.agentFloatLowWatermarkMinor;
  return { currencyCode, balanceMinor: balanceMinor.toString(), balance: formatMinorToDecimal(balanceMinor), lowWatermarkMinor: watermark.toString(), isLow: balanceMinor < watermark, checkedAt: new Date().toISOString() };
Add as `@Get('agent-float')` on ReconciliationController beside the existing `@Post('agent-float/sync')`, with @AdminAuth(...VIEW_ROLES).

gaps.requestShape:
enum PlayerSource {
  /// The ordinary case — the player pressed Start.
  TELEGRAM
  /// An account that already existed under the operator's Ichancy agent before the bot did.
  ICHANCY_IMPORT
  /// A row registered from the console.
  ADMIN
  @@map("player_source")
}

// changed on model Player:
  telegramUserId BigInt? @map("telegram_user_id")   /// was BigInt @unique
  source PlayerSource @default(TELEGRAM)
  @@unique([tenantId, telegramUserId])              /// replaces the global @unique

// enum PlayerStatus gains:
  /// The operator's own lock. Not an Ichancy state — the casino account is untouched.
  BLOCKED

// added to model Player:
  /// All three set together while status is BLOCKED, and all three null otherwise.
  blockedAt DateTime? @map("blocked_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  blockedReason String? @map("blocked_reason")      /// 1..280
  blockedByAdminId String? @map("blocked_by_admin_id") @db.Uuid
  blockedByAdmin AdminUser? @relation("PlayerBlockedBy", fields: [blockedByAdminId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  @@index([tenantId, status, createdAt])

// model TelegramUpdate:
  tenantId String @map("tenant_id") @db.Uuid
  tenant Tenant @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  @@index([tenantId, receivedAt])
  /// updateId stays GLOBALLY unique — Telegram's id space is global and a replayed approve
  /// callback must never approve twice, whichever bot it arrived on.

// enum BreakCategory gains:
  /// Debited and nobody was paid, past the operator's tolerance.
  STUCK_WITHDRAWAL
  /// A payout was recorded twice against one withdrawal.
  DUPLICATE_PAYOUT
  /// A chain transfer we saw that no deposit claims.
  UNMATCHED_CHAIN_TRANSFER
